# ============================================================
# plan: gevs_unit -- NASA GEVS thermal vacuum, unit level, protoflight
# ============================================================
# Eight cycles between -30 and 60 °C under high vacuum, as NASA's General
# Environmental Verification Standard asks of a unit (GSFC-STD-7000B, 2.6.3;
# memory/use/gevs.md). The article sits on the platen, powered from psu1 CH2.
#
# The numbers, and where they come from:
#   -30 and 60 °C   the article's allowable flight range, -20 to 50 °C, plus 10 °C
#                   each way (protoflight; qualification is 15, acceptance 5).
#                   Change the plateau, rule and guard lines together.
#   1e-5 Torr       below it, gas conduction is negligible (2.6.2.4.4).
#   1 °C/min        the fastest transition GEVS suggests (Table 2.6-1).
#   2 °C            a plateau starts when the platen is within it (2.6.3.2.3).
#   4 h, 2 h        each plateau with the article on, and each with it off.
#   8 cycles        the unit level's share of the 12 before flight (Table 2.6-1).
#   5 V, 1 A        the article's supply, protected at 5.5 V and 1.2 A: set yours.
# The first cycle starts the article cold, then hot, each after 2 hours off
# (2.6.3.3.1.5). The log says when to run the article's functional test.
#
# Start: ambient. The chamber at atmosphere with its door closed, the platen and
#   shroud between 10 and 60 °C, liquid nitrogen supplied, the article on psu1 CH2.
# End:   at atmosphere, the vent valve open. Both zones off, every pump off, the
#   article's supply off.
# Fails: the chamber is not at atmosphere at the start, does not reach 1e-5 Torr
#   within 8 hours, the platen does not reach a plateau within 3 hours, or the
#   chamber does not return to air.
#
# Takes about 4 days: 8 cycles of about 11 hours. The turbo pump path (highvac)
# has not yet been run on this chamber: run highvac and seal chamber on their own,
# watched at the HMI, before the first full test. Cooling uses liquid nitrogen
# throughout; its exhaust must be vented outside the building.

load rLACO rPSU rSMTC08
record every 30 s

when platenT > 65 C then hvc platen off
when platenT < -35 C then hvc platen off

begin at ambient
psu1 ch2 off
psu1 ch2 set 5.0 1.0
psu1 ch2 protect 5.5 1.2
hvc platen rate 1
hvc shroud rate 1
highvac to 0.00001 Torr within 8 h
when chamberP > 0.0001 then log vacuum lost: above 1e-4 Torr

# Cycle 1: cold start, then hot start
plateau at -30 C within 180 min
log cold soak with the article off
hold 2 h
psu1 ch2 on
log cold turn-on: check the article, then run its functional test
hold 4 h
plateau at 60 C within 180 min
psu1 ch2 off
log hot soak with the article off
hold 2 h
psu1 ch2 on
log hot turn-on: check the article, then run its functional test
hold 4 h

# Cycles 2 to 8, the article on throughout
repeat 7 times
  plateau at -30 C within 180 min
  log cold plateau: run the article's functional test
  hold 4 h
  plateau at 60 C within 180 min
  log hot plateau: run the article's functional test
  hold 4 h
end

# Back to air, the platen held warmer than the shroud until the chamber is at air
plateau at 30 C within 180 min
hvc shroud 25
psu1 ch2 off
seal chamber
vent within 60 min
hvc platen off
hvc shroud off
log GEVS unit test done: 8 cycles, back at atmosphere
